Brazilian territorial meshes and hierarchy
-------------------------------------------

The bundled territorial geometries, geographic identifiers and territorial
hierarchy are derived from data published by the Brazilian Institute of
Geography and Statistics (Instituto Brasileiro de Geografia e Estatística,
IBGE).

Primary sources:

* IBGE municipal mesh archive:
  https://geoftp.ibge.gov.br/organizacao_do_territorio/malhas_territoriais/malhas_municipais/
* IBGE Localities API:
  https://servicodados.ibge.gov.br/api/docs/localidades
* IBGE open data information:
  https://www.ibge.gov.br/acesso-informacao/dados-abertos.html

The package author selected the bundled editions, standardized fields and
coordinate reference systems, repaired invalid geometries, simplified the
municipal meshes and encoded the installed objects as compressed TopoJSON.
The exact source URLs and checksums for municipal editions are installed in
maps/municipality/index.csv.

The state_hex and state_region cartograms are curated representations created
for this package from official state identifiers. They are not official IBGE
territorial boundaries.

Example datasets
----------------

The gini2015 and pop2017 example datasets are derived from data published by
IBGE. The deaths example dataset is derived from data published by DATASUS,
the Informatics Department of the Brazilian Unified Health System.

Attribution of the original data remains with the respective public
institutions. Inclusion in brazilmaps does not imply endorsement by IBGE or
DATASUS. Users should consult the source institutions for the terms and
metadata applicable to the original datasets.
